md=['# Post-seal historical comparison','',f'Created {now}. Current frozen target: `{identity["r001"]}`.','', 'This is a separately authorized history-exposed follow-up after the independent first passes. Historical material was not supplied to active cold reviewers. No old proof was replayed, no new exploit research was run and no production code was edited. The comparison preserves what the documents claim; it does not authenticate every historic execution or import historical owner acceptance into this round.','', '## What changes in the interpretation','', '**The two main r001 mechanisms have prior history.** V12 IDs `243747` and `243754` already describe forged or subsequently unavailable prizes with independent sponsor/treasury payouts. IDs `243748`, `243749` and `243759` describe future-clone self-stranding; `243750` describes the treasury-nonce creation trap. The r001 reports add current-source assessment and an honest-token recipient reproduction, not a basis for claiming these mechanism families were previously unknown.','', '**Historical closure depends on the old architecture.** August 9 H-03/H-04 were called fixed by adding `recoverProtocolOwnedClaim`. August 13 ES-01 then records that helper as a theft surface when a permissionless future address is captured, and removes it. It is absent now. H-01/H-02 self-address checks remain conceptually present, but the future-address gap cannot be called resolved by that obsolete helper. Do not revive the helper without a fresh ownership/recipient design review.','', '**The old failed-prize fallback is not current behavior.** ES-03 reports retaining gross proceeds and opening full refunds after 30 days in an earlier Base/Pyth design. Later Ethereum risk ledgers explicitly describe independent proceeds and no post-result refund. Current RF-001 keeps its scope disagreement. A historical “accepted dependency risk” or “owner decision” is not current user acceptance, and a changed design is not automatically an accidental regression.','', '**Quote accounting intentionally changed.** August 24 retained exact balance deltas. The August 25 trusted-USDC follow-up explicitly supersedes that policy and matches r001 nominal SafeERC20 transfers. Thus V12 `243757` and early ledger exact-delta claims do not describe this freeze. The same follow-up expressly preserves old mutation definitions without claiming the historical 52/52 score for the changed source. AQ-006 remains a current-target assurance gap, with this provenance qualification.','', '## Historical identities','', '| Document family | Recorded identity |','|---|---|']
